import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.SecondHurewiczSimplyConnectedTriangleGluedRecovery
import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.SecondHurewiczSimplyConnectedTetrahedron

/-!
# Based triangles and tetrahedra in the native second homotopy group

An actual singular triangle with based boundary defines a native generalized
loop. Its Hurewicz image is the original singular triangle minus the constant
triangle in the unnormalized complex. An actual based-one-skeleton tetrahedron
gives the signed four-face relation. Coherent homotopies of the two original
square triangles recover their native class with exactly the square-chain
signs, using explicit relative homotopies and diagonal subdivision.

These results hold for arbitrary topological spaces. They do not assert a
Hurewicz isomorphism or a sphere-recognition theorem.
-/
